# 100 Days of Cloud AWS — Final Task
# AWS EC2 EBS Volume Expansion (8 GiB to 12 GiB)

## Project Overview

The Nautilus DevOps Team identified that its development EC2 instance, `devops-ec2`, was running out of storage space.

The instance had an attached root EBS volume with an initial capacity of 8 GiB. The objective was to expand the volume to 12 GiB and ensure that the additional storage became available within the running Linux instance.

The task involved identifying the attached EBS volume, modifying its capacity through the AWS CLI, connecting to the instance using SSH, expanding the root partition, and growing the XFS filesystem.

**Result:** Successfully expanded the EBS volume, root partition, and root filesystem from 8 GiB to 12 GiB without rebooting the EC2 instance.

## Project Objectives

- Identify the EBS volume attached to `devops-ec2`.
- Increase the EBS volume size from 8 GiB to 12 GiB.
- Use AWS CLI to manage the storage modification.
- Connect to the EC2 instance using SSH.
- Expand the Linux root partition.
- Extend the XFS filesystem.
- Verify that the root filesystem recognizes the new capacity.

